cff-version: 1.2.0
type: software
message: "If you use FRACMATH, cite the immutable code commit identified in the SoftwareX manuscript."
title: "FRACMATH: A vectorized MATLAB framework for continuum damage mechanics with crack band regularization"
authors:
  - family-names: Mavani
    given-names: Jaykumar
    email: jaymavani9033@gmail.com
  - family-names: Pathirage
    given-names: Madura
    email: mpathirage@unm.edu
repository-code: "https://github.com/Jaykumar9033/FRACMATH"
version: "1.1.0-dev"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - fracture mechanics
  - continuum damage mechanics
  - crack-band regularization
  - finite element method
  - MATLAB
  - Abaqus
  - UMAT
abstract: >-
  FRACMATH is a MATLAB framework for finite element simulation of fracture in
  quasibrittle materials using scalar isotropic continuum damage mechanics,
  modified von Mises equivalent strain, exponential softening, and
  direction-dependent Oliver crack-band regularization.
